<title>ITALY: Italy says revised 1996 deficit 127.5 trln lire.</title>
<headline>Italy says revised 1996 deficit 127.5 trln lire.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said on Monday that Italy's revised 1996 deficit was 127.5 trillion lire ($76.8 billion) after rulings from the EU's Eurostat.</p>
<p>He told a news conference the 1996 deficit to gross domestic product ratio was 6.81 percent.</p>
</text>
